@@section 1
@@title First-tick water drops no items, 2026-10-27 ([perf.md](../perf.md) 10.6, TODO `perf #14`)
@@date 2026-10-27
@@jars creativecommon creativeworldgen
@@sources feature_writeup/perf.md
@@text
@@text Target: patcherMod 1.1.03 installed in `mods/` 2026-10-27 13:22 (also carries the Armor Trims cache above); copy it into
@@text the scratch `mods/`. Two fresh group B worlds on the eval seed -8188900049893920259 (`tools/perf/eval/eval_server.sh setup`
@@text works, JFR optional): `ftw_on` as shipped, `ftw_off` with `[worldgen.systems] firstTickWater = false` in
@@text `config/creativeengineering-common.toml` before boot. Run the same commands in both, one server at a time. Count with
@@text `python3 tools/perf/eval/entity_census.py OUT/srv/LEVEL` after `stop`. Baseline from the eval (perf.md 10.2 #5): 672 item
@@text entities at spawn (299 moss carpet, 65 wheat seeds, 53 azalea, 42 hemp seeds, 16 torches) and 227 falling blocks.
@@text The water still flows as in vanilla in both worlds; only the items differ.
@@text
@@text | ID | World | Commands | Expected | If it fails |
@@text |---|---|---|---|---|
## SQ-FTW-01
@group B `ftw_on`
@commands Boot; grep latest.log for `FlowingFluidSettleMixin`, `LevelChunkFirstTickWaterMixin`, `BlockPopResourceSettleMixin`, `m_152440_`, `m_62812_`; check `config/creativeengineering-common.toml` has `[worldgen.first_tick_water]` `windowTicks = 600`
@pass No mixin warning or error; `Done` time within the eval's 212-225 s (no startup cost)
@fails Injection failure on `m_152440_`: another mod changed `Block.popResource` (grep `exported/` / mixin audit for `popResource`)
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootexpect Done \(
bootreject (Mixin apply failed|InvalidInjectionException|Critical injection failure|InjectionError).*(FlowingFluidSettleMixin|LevelChunkFirstTickWaterMixin|BlockPopResourceSettleMixin|m_152440_|m_62812_)
bootreject (?i)(WARN|ERROR).*(FlowingFluidSettleMixin|LevelChunkFirstTickWaterMixin|BlockPopResourceSettleMixin)
shell grep -A4 "first_tick_water" config/creativeworldgen-common.toml | grep -E "windowTicks"; grep -oE "Done \([0-9.]+s\)" logs/latest.log
look windowTicks = 600 under [worldgen.first_tick_water] (the section moved to creativeworldgen-common.toml); the Done time against 212-225 s on this machine (no startup cost)
## SQ-FTW-02 | ftw_on: item entities after the spawn chunks ticked 120 s
@group same, then `ftw_off`
@commands After `Done` `/cdevtest tickwarp 2400` (was a 120 s wait: the spawn chunks tick), `save-all flush`, census
@pass `ftw_on`: item entities below y 50 near 0 (moss carpet, seeds, azalea, glow berries, torches, cocoa, Miner's Delight plants each under 10); `ftw_off`: about the eval's 672. Falling blocks may stay in both
@fails Still hundreds in `ftw_on`: note which items and their y; sugar cane / cactus / bamboo are expected leftovers (scheduled support ticks, perf.md 10.6); others lying near no water point to a second cause
@from batches/r1103w/w_9_B.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootexpect Done \(
> cdevtest tickwarp 2400
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done 240
> save-all flush
waitlog Saved the game 300
shell mkdir -p $INST/perf/runs/r1103w/w; rm -rf ../ftw_on_snap; mkdir ../ftw_on_snap && cp -r ftw_on/entities ../ftw_on_snap/ && python3 -I $INST/tools/perf/eval/entity_census.py ../ftw_on_snap > $INST/perf/runs/r1103w/w/ftw_on_census.txt 2>&1; head -40 $INST/perf/runs/r1103w/w/ftw_on_census.txt
look item entities near 0 (moss carpet, seeds, azalea, glow berries, torches, cocoa, Miner's plants each under 10; sugar cane / cactus / bamboo expected leftovers); the ftw_off half is w_10_B.qb; baseline 672 items (perf.md 10.2 #5)

## SQ-FTW-03
@group same pair
@commands Pregen without ticking: `/chunky center 4000 4000`, `/chunky radius 120`, `/chunky start`, wait for done; then `/forceload add 3888 3888 4112 4112`, wait 90 s, `/forceload remove all`, wait 10 s, `stop`, census
@pass `ftw_on` well under `ftw_off` for the cave plant items
@fails Equal counts: forceloaded chunks did not tick fluids (then rely on SQ-FTW-02)
@reviewed 2026-11-16
# run on the ftw_on boot, then again on ftw_off (the pair as SQ-FTW-02)
> chunky center 4000 4000
> chunky radius 120
> chunky start
waitlog (?i)\[chunky\] task finished|generation.*complete|100(\.0+)?% 900
> forceload add 3888 3888 4112 4112
> cdevtest tickwarp 1800
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done 300
> forceload remove all
> cdevtest tickwarp 200
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=200 120
> save-all flush
waitlog Saved the game 300
shell L=$(grep -E "^level-name=" server.properties | cut -d= -f2); rm -rf ../ftw3_snap_$L; mkdir ../ftw3_snap_$L && cp -r $L/entities ../ftw3_snap_$L/ && python3 -I $INST/tools/perf/eval/entity_census.py ../ftw3_snap_$L 2>&1 | head -40
look cave plant items (moss carpet, azalea, glow berries, Miner's Delight plants) on ftw_on well under ftw_off; equal counts mean the forceloaded chunks did not tick fluids (then rely on SQ-FTW-02)
## SQ-FTW-04
@group A
@commands Boot, stay at spawn 60 s. `/kill @e[type=item]`, `/setblock ~3 ~ ~ minecraft:grass`, `/setblock ~2 ~ ~ minecraft:water`; after 2 s `/execute if block ~3 ~ ~ minecraft:grass` and `/execute if entity @e[type=item,distance=..8]`
@pass Vanilla after the window: the grass is washed away and items may lie there (grass drops seeds 1 time in 8: repeat with a torch, `/setblock ~3 ~ ~ minecraft:torch`, which always drops)
@fails Torch washed with no item: the window never closed (purge or `windowTicks` check)
@reviewed 2026-11-16
# spawn chunks are older than windowTicks 600 after this warp: vanilla washing (the torch always drops)
> pbot spawn ftw 0 -60 0 minecraft:overworld creative
> cdevtest tickwarp 1200
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done 120
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item]
> setblock 3 -60 0 minecraft:torch
> setblock 2 -60 0 minecraft:water
sleep 3
> execute if block 3 -60 0 minecraft:torch run say FTW04 torch still there
> execute positioned 3 -60 0 if entity @e[type=minecraft:item,nbt={Item:{id:"minecraft:torch"}},distance=..8] run say FTW04 torch item
expect FTW04 torch item
reject FTW04 torch still there
reject \[cdevtest\] verb=\S+ done=0
## SQ-FTW-05 | fresh chunk 2000 away, inside the window: torch washed away, no torch item
@group same
@commands Fresh chunk 2000 blocks away: `/tp @s 2000 ~ 2000`; within 20 s `/kill @e[type=item]`, `/setblock ~3 ~ ~ minecraft:torch`, `/setblock ~2 ~ ~ minecraft:water`; after 2 s check block and items as above
@pass Torch washed away, no torch item (inside the window, perf.md 10.6 side effect)
@fails Torch item present: the chunk window is not opened (`postProcessGeneration` hook or `InhabitedTime` test)
@from batches/r1103w/w_5_A.qb
> pbot spawn ftw 0 -60 0 minecraft:overworld creative
sleep 3
> tp ftw 2000 -60 2000
sleep 4
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item]
> setblock 2003 -60 2000 minecraft:torch
> setblock 2002 -60 2000 minecraft:water
sleep 3
> execute if block 2003 -60 2000 minecraft:torch run say FTW05 torch still there
> execute positioned 2003 -60 2000 if entity @e[type=minecraft:item,distance=..8] run say FTW05 item present
> execute positioned 2003 -60 2000 unless entity @e[type=minecraft:item,distance=..8] run say FTW05 no item
expect FTW05 no item
reject FTW05 torch still there
reject FTW05 item present
# superflat: grass at y -61, so a torch at y -60 stands on it; the whole step must finish inside windowTicks 600 (30 s) of the chunk first ticking

## SQ-FTW-06 | windowTicks 0: the torch item drops (no window)
@group same
@commands Set `[worldgen.first_tick_water] windowTicks = 0` in the scratch config (applies at once, or restart); repeat SQ-FTW-05 at `/tp @s -2000 ~ -2000`
@pass The torch item drops (no window)
@fails No item: the 0 value is not read (`WorldgenConfig.firstTickWaterWindowTicks`)
@from batches/r1103w/w_6_A.qb
shell grep -nE '^\s*windowTicks = 0' config/creativeworldgen-common.toml
> pbot spawn ftw 0 -60 0 minecraft:overworld creative
sleep 3
> tp ftw -2000 -60 -2000
sleep 4
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item]
> setblock -1997 -60 -2000 minecraft:torch
> setblock -1998 -60 -2000 minecraft:water
sleep 3
> execute positioned -1997 -60 -2000 if entity @e[type=minecraft:item,nbt={Item:{id:"minecraft:torch"}},distance=..8] run say FTW06 torch item
> execute positioned -1997 -60 -2000 unless entity @e[type=minecraft:item,distance=..8] run say FTW06 no item
expect FTW06 torch item
reject FTW06 no item

